1. Andrej Karpathy — prompting philosophy
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
P2P's "Template M" (also surfaced as the `/p2p-karpathy` command and the
`p2p-karpathy` skill, "Karpathy Mode") was inspired by Andrej Karpathy's
public observations on LLM coding pitfalls and minimalist prompting:

  - "The models make wrong assumptions on your behalf and just run along with
     them without checking. They don't manage their confusion, don't seek
     clarifications, don't surface inconsistencies, don't present tradeoffs,
     don't push back when they should."
  - "They really like to overcomplicate code and APIs, bloat abstractions..."
  - "Best prompt — no prompt, only clean context."

Source post: https://x.com/karpathy/status/2015883857489522876 (and adjacent
threads on @karpathy's X account).

Andrej Karpathy is credited as the originator of the underlying philosophy.
P2P's implementation (Template M, PRE_CODE_DECLARATION, surgical-change rules
inside `.claude/skills/p2p-karpathy/`) is independently authored. No source
code from Andrej Karpathy is bundled in this repository.

